# SFT execution status v0.74

2026-09-10. **HF checkpoint save/reload and explicit config/runtime-code content
reads are now byte-budgeted in a new CPU-kernel successor.** Tiny BF16, FP32,
untied and sharded roundtrips pass. This completes v0.73's HF/control-content-I/O
software task, not coordinator integration, host admission or all of Gate 5.

No real weights, trainer/tokenizer payloads or datasets were read. No GPU,
inference, training, network action, installation, instance action, GitHub push
or CI was initiated. Frozen predecessors and their evidence remain unchanged.

## Implemented

`posttraining_checkpoint_hf_io_v1.py` owns separate, caller-chosen logical read
and write ledgers. Each at-most-1-MiB `pread`/`pwrite` reserves requested bytes
before the syscall; failed reservations are not refunded. Control files are
read through pinned, no-follow descriptors, without changing their existing
0400/0600/0644 modes. Output uses a fresh exclusive 0700 directory and 0600
files. Reads bind the exact write receipt, size, hash and recorded identity.
Inventory checks metadata and recorded receipts; it does not hide extra content
rereads. Failure poisons the session, and a late close/budget failure prevents
the enclosing kernel from returning success. Partial output is not reused.

`posttraining_checkpoint_hf_bytes_v1.py` uses the public safetensors bytes APIs
one bounded shard at a time. Before tensor deserialization it validates exact
keys, dtype, shapes, alias policy, offsets and complete nonoverlapping extents.
Only the configured, exactly shared embedding/head alias is omitted. Shard,
index and configuration files remain compatible with the ordinary HF loader.

`posttraining_checkpoint_import_torch_v5.py` reuses the frozen v0.73 DCP reader.
It routes the source configuration and two runtime-code control reads, generated
files and HF verification reads through the new content session. The actual HF
`from_pretrained` receives in-memory state, configuration and generation objects,
with no checkpoint pathname. The implementation does not patch library globals
or use native pathname checkpoint serialization/loading.

Before output creation, it checks conservative serialized writes, all planned
HF/control reads and visible serialization scratch against explicit caller
caps. Scratch is four times the largest serialized-shard bound plus 2 MiB,
included in the live projection alongside two cast states. This does not measure
RSS or prove native allocator bounds; it does not silently raise the existing
real-plan memory allowance. Source key/shape/chunk checks, finite-value checks,
independent tied-alias validation, casts, FP32 buffers, config preservation and
complete HF tensor equality/digest checks remain. The receipt is explicitly v0.5.

## Verification

**549 distinct tests pass in the targeted suites, with no failures or skips.**
This is not a full-repository or real-checkpoint qualification claim.

- 464 stdlib tests on Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7 and 3.14.6: 0.825s, 0.788s and
  0.865s. This includes all of v0.73's 414 stdlib regressions.
- 85 genuine tiny CPU tests on Python 3.13.7: 1.185s test time and 3.054s
  supervised wall time under a 60-second parent timeout. All 71 prior native
  regressions remain included.
- 64 new tests: 41 content-session, nine source/header and 14 native integration.
- Ruff E,F,I,B,UP / py311 / line length 100 passes on all six new code/test files.
  Existing Torch DCP/platform/deprecation warnings remain visible.

Tests exercise BF16/FP32/untied conversion, multiple shards and independent stock
HF filename-loader compatibility. That last compatibility read is explicitly
test-only and outside the kernel receipt. A separate success test disables
native path save/safetensors opening. Intercepted HF/control `pread`/`pwrite`
request sizes exactly match the reported counters. Limit tests deny output
before serialization, corrupted output is rejected before loading, and close
failure cannot report success. The initial development issue was Torch returning
an `OrderedDict`: the helper now accepts exactly `dict` or `OrderedDict` and
copies the mapping. No validation gate was weakened to make a test pass.

Report: `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-import-metered-hf-v0.1.json`.
Structural verification:
`evidence/lumi-4b-sft-import-metered-hf-verification-v0.1.json`.

## Remaining work

1. Version coordinator/package integration for the v0.5 kernel and combine the
   explicit ledgers. Reuse/account for the DCP reader's audit within the existing
   two-audit plan; do not silently add a third full audit or increase saved caps.
   The frozen coordinator/package deliberately still require old evidence and
   are not wired to this successor.
2. Integrate and qualify the Linux guardian/cgroup and filesystem/network/write
   controls, then admit the exact native host/runtime and resource plan. Mac
   tests do not qualify Linux enforcement. Real DCP inputs still must satisfy
   the frozen reader's 0600/0700 contract; compatibility with existing 0400 DCP
   inputs has not been established, and no input was chmodded.
3. Only after those prerequisites and exact execution authorization, perform the
   real checkpoint import and downstream GPU worker/profile, data relocation and
   CUDA/smoke work already recorded in v0.70-v0.73. This is not authorization to
   launch them now.

The new ledgers cover explicit checkpoint/control content, not dependency/module
imports, physical disk I/O, hard timeouts, all process writes or native RSS.
Metadata pickle still requires trusted hash-bound inputs; hashing is not safe
unpickling, origin proof or atomic protection from a hostile owner.

No GPU is needed for the next software integration step. Public `run_import`
still fails closed with `host_guard_not_bound`. **Gate 5 remains incomplete;
real SFT, execution permission and production eligibility remain false.** The
S3-backed pretrained base and all dataset/rights/evaluation rules are unchanged.

HEAD remains `ecc545fc423650bf1089311915290523c10b3172`, with empty tracked and
staged diffs. This stage adds three modules, three test files, a report,
structural verification and this status successor, all local/unpublished.
